# GitHub language statistics (Linguist).
#
# Two corrections, and neither hides code. The shell suite stays counted:
# bench/ is the evidence behind the README's claims, and "22% Shell" is an
# accurate description of this repository rather than an embarrassment to be
# attributed away.

# These are Tanod YAML configs with @PLACEHOLDER@ substitution, rendered by
# bench_render_config. Linguist maps the .tpl extension to Go Template on the
# name alone and never opens the file — there is no Go in this repository.
*.yaml.tpl linguist-language=YAML

# A Next.js storefront that exists to be a target for bench/nextjs.sh and
# bench/nextjs-browser.sh. It is the thing under protection in those tests, not
# part of Tanod, and it is counted out of the language bar for the same
# reason a bundled example app usually is.
fixtures/** linguist-vendored
